WEBVTT

00:01.970 --> 00:04.230
Mom won't be home tonight.

00:04.230 --> 00:07.230
Cool. And thanks for this, Ozu.

00:07.820 --> 00:12.700
Are you sure you want your little sister 
having a guest over at midnight, though?

00:13.190 --> 00:14.940
It's a little late to worry about that.

00:15.970 --> 00:19.700
Like I keep telling you, 
I don't have a sister complex.

00:19.700 --> 00:24.250
If you two were to get together, 
I'd be excited to see your kids.

00:24.250 --> 00:26.570
That's kind of messed up in its own way.

00:26.570 --> 00:29.160
Find some more respectable interests, okay?

00:29.160 --> 00:31.260
I'm forever trying.

00:33.030 --> 00:34.510
I wish you luck.

00:35.060 --> 00:36.660
Well, I'm off.

00:48.180 --> 00:49.860
Hey, Iroha.

00:49.860 --> 00:52.990
You're awake, aren't you? I want to talk.

00:56.980 --> 00:59.620
I know you don't go to bed this early!

01:00.020 --> 01:01.640
Answer me already!

01:01.640 --> 01:04.940
Jeez, you never give up! 
What do you want?

01:06.630 --> 01:09.060
I want to talk about 
what happened at the studio.

01:09.060 --> 01:10.320
Would you open the door?

01:11.460 --> 01:15.070
Taking advantage of my mom being out 
to barge in and lecture me?

01:15.070 --> 01:18.050
It's not that. I just want to apologize to you.

01:18.050 --> 01:21.890
Apologize? It's not like I'm angry or anything.

01:22.440 --> 01:27.140
If anything, you're the one who's angry 
at me for blowing the recording.

01:27.520 --> 01:29.060
I'm not angry—

01:30.090 --> 01:33.660
No. It's true that I did get angry back there.

01:33.660 --> 01:35.740
But rather than acknowledging my own weakness,

01:36.300 --> 01:38.380
I took my anger out on you.

01:39.120 --> 01:40.070
That's why...

01:41.310 --> 01:42.740
I'm here to apologize.

01:42.740 --> 01:44.870
I don't need an apology!

01:45.220 --> 01:48.750
I'm not in the mood to see you 
right now! Just go home!

01:48.750 --> 01:51.620
What kind of mood you're in doesn't matter!

01:51.620 --> 01:53.530
Just talk to me, damn it!

01:53.530 --> 01:55.440
No way!

01:56.130 --> 01:59.630
You're just gonna try to win me over 
with your magical conversational skills!

01:59.630 --> 02:02.210
I know your seduction methods inside and out!

02:02.210 --> 02:04.380
I'm not opening that door! No way!

02:05.250 --> 02:07.280
Enough of this! I told you to open up!

02:07.280 --> 02:09.270
If you don't, I'll break the door down!

02:09.270 --> 02:13.650
If it were that easy for anyone to break down 
a door, kickboxers would be out of a job!

02:13.650 --> 02:15.260
Are you sure about that?

02:15.260 --> 02:17.280
Go ahead and try it, then!

02:17.280 --> 02:18.540
If you say so.

02:28.050 --> 02:29.000
Huh?

02:53.650 --> 02:59.320
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

03:59.630 --> 04:04.590
<b>#10 "MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER
ONLY GETS AN APOLOGY FROM ME"</b>

03:59.750 --> 04:01.710
First, here's some money to fix the door.

04:02.090 --> 04:05.470
You can't run away now. 
You're going to hear me out, Iroha.

04:05.470 --> 04:07.980
I can't believe you actually broke my door.

04:07.980 --> 04:10.100
Could you be any more irrational?

04:10.100 --> 04:13.260
I don't think someone who regularly 
enters my room without permission

04:13.260 --> 04:14.620
has any right to complain.

04:15.100 --> 04:18.650
How do you manage to be so overbearing 
even while you're groveling?

04:19.790 --> 04:23.500
I will apologize, but I will also 
refute what needs to be refuted.

04:23.500 --> 04:25.110
That's my style.

04:25.110 --> 04:27.290
You're ridiculous.

04:27.290 --> 04:28.620
Anyway, I have news for you.

04:28.970 --> 04:31.540
I just saw Mashiro and turned her down.

04:32.940 --> 04:36.630
Oh? Why'd you go and do that?

04:36.920 --> 04:41.630
That might have been your 
last chance to lose your virginity.

04:41.630 --> 04:44.040
I intended to turn her down all along.

04:45.010 --> 04:48.660
To be honest, I've never even thought 
about romance before,

04:48.660 --> 04:51.710
so I never looked at her that way.

04:51.710 --> 04:54.020
But, even though I didn't realize it,

04:54.810 --> 04:57.180
I think I let it go to my head.

04:57.650 --> 05:00.440
Oh, you did, did you?

05:00.440 --> 05:01.030
Yes.

05:01.810 --> 05:05.670
Even after I swore that I'd take my work 
with 05th Floor Alliance seriously,

05:05.670 --> 05:07.280
I got careless.

05:07.280 --> 05:09.660
That's why you're angry, right?

05:11.390 --> 05:15.020
I had thrown away my adolescence, 
romance... everything.

05:15.740 --> 05:18.060
So please give me another chance.

05:18.420 --> 05:25.670
I'll give my all to producing Kohinata Iroha,
no, everyone in 05th Floor Alliance.

05:26.040 --> 05:26.890
So...

05:31.100 --> 05:35.430
So don't be dishonest with me when you 
feel negatively about something.

05:39.690 --> 05:43.940
You're half right and half off the mark.

05:43.940 --> 05:45.250
Half?

05:45.250 --> 05:48.460
Weren't you going to dedicate 
everything to 05th Floor Alliance?

05:48.460 --> 05:54.200
You were contradicting yourself... 
which was part of it, I guess.

05:54.560 --> 05:59.170
But I can't be as stoic about things as you.

05:59.170 --> 06:01.460
I'm just an ordinary high school girl.

06:04.740 --> 06:07.510
Of course I get... jealous.

06:07.510 --> 06:08.180
Huh?

06:08.750 --> 06:13.260
You didn't have anyone 
outside 05th Floor Alliance,

06:13.260 --> 06:18.170
and you never got close enough to anyone 
to call them a friend, except for my brother.

06:18.990 --> 06:25.610
The truth is, you only take us seriously
when work is involved.

06:26.030 --> 06:27.180
That's not...

06:27.530 --> 06:30.900
You're always saying it, aren't you?

06:30.900 --> 06:33.340
That you'll make 05th Floor Alliance a success,

06:33.340 --> 06:36.830
and that you'll find the quickest, 
most efficient route to making that happen.

06:37.270 --> 06:40.670
And that you don't want any of us 
to expect anything more of you.

06:41.110 --> 06:44.000
That's exactly what you said that day.

06:44.750 --> 06:49.220
<i>She's right. That's the promise I made 
when I started 05th Floor Alliance.</i>

06:49.220 --> 06:53.330
<i>No... I know my obsession 
with efficiency has hurt people.</i>

06:53.330 --> 06:57.010
<i>That's why I can't get closer 
than necessary to anyone</i>

06:57.010 --> 06:59.750
<i>as long as I'm the leader of the group.</i>

07:00.270 --> 07:03.400
<i>If anyone got hurt, 
05th Floor Alliance would collapse.</i>

07:04.200 --> 07:05.520
<i>And yet...</i>

07:08.220 --> 07:09.100
<i>I...</i>

07:10.200 --> 07:14.920
You got close with Mashiro-senpai, 
even though she's not in 05th Floor Alliance.

07:15.450 --> 07:19.980
You took her confession seriously, 
even though it had nothing to do with work.

07:20.610 --> 07:22.700
It made me wonder 
what happened to the distance

07:22.700 --> 07:25.830
you always kept between yourself and others.

07:26.260 --> 07:29.340
Frankly, I was like, "What the hell?"

07:29.340 --> 07:32.650
Mashiro and I... have our own circumstances.

07:33.030 --> 07:37.850
She's not in 05th Floor Alliance, but she 
needs the same amount of my attention.

07:37.850 --> 07:41.730
If I don't keep up our fake relationship, 
none of us will get hired.

07:42.140 --> 07:45.360
But there was more to it, wasn't there?

07:48.950 --> 07:52.540
Sorry. I know it's not your fault.

07:52.540 --> 07:56.490
No one could've avoided 
a direct approach like that.

07:56.810 --> 08:00.490
I know that... just as well 
as anyone, you know.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.240
Iroha...

08:05.500 --> 08:07.670
And that's why I've been jealous!

08:07.980 --> 08:12.360
I was jealous of Mashiro-senpai because 
you took her seriously outside of work!

08:12.360 --> 08:14.420
So I just couldn't help myself!

08:14.420 --> 08:18.770
I thought maybe if I acted out while working, 
you'd take <i>me</i> seriously for a change!

08:18.770 --> 08:20.680
I was acting like a spoiled brat!

08:20.680 --> 08:21.680
So...

08:21.680 --> 08:23.080
I'm sorry!

08:27.100 --> 08:29.370
Jealous, huh?

08:29.370 --> 08:34.540
I... never expected to hear that 
coming from you.

08:36.020 --> 08:38.430
Let me make sure I have this right.

08:38.430 --> 08:39.920
You felt jealous...

08:42.330 --> 08:46.090
in a romantic sense?

09:07.880 --> 09:12.030
I just got a super-cute sound bite out of you!

09:12.030 --> 09:13.050
Wha...

09:13.050 --> 09:15.960
Don't tell me... you just...

09:15.960 --> 09:17.910
<i>Let me make sure I have this right.</i>

09:17.910 --> 09:19.440
<i>You felt jealous...</i>

09:19.440 --> 09:20.660
<i>in a romantic sense?</i>

09:20.660 --> 09:22.770
What's this? What's this, now?

09:22.770 --> 09:26.540
You were worried about whether my jealousy 
was based on <i>romantic</i> feelings?

09:26.540 --> 09:30.170
Were you so worried it kept you up at night?

09:30.170 --> 09:34.170
That can't be anything but love, can it?!

09:34.170 --> 09:36.700
You... That's not what I meant!

09:36.700 --> 09:38.180
<i>You felt jealous...</i>

09:38.180 --> 09:40.290
<i>in a romantic sense?</i>

09:40.290 --> 09:42.180
Stop it!

09:42.900 --> 09:46.810
Jealousy isn't always about 
romantic feelings, you know.

09:46.810 --> 09:52.400
It's possible to feel jealous when 
your friend gets close to another friend.

09:52.400 --> 09:57.070
Humans feel jealousy over all sorts of things.

09:57.070 --> 10:00.330
Oh! But you don't have many friends, do you?

10:00.330 --> 10:03.340
So you wouldn't know! Sorry!

10:03.340 --> 10:04.830
Damn, you're a pain!

10:05.220 --> 10:07.380
Come on, at least erase that recording!

10:07.380 --> 10:09.830
That's not going to happen!

10:10.120 --> 10:13.750
It's not often you give me a glimpse 
of a weakness <i>this</i> tasty!

10:14.030 --> 10:18.010
You know what'll happen if you let 
the others hear that, don't you?

10:18.010 --> 10:20.450
Oh? What <i>will</i> happen?

10:20.450 --> 10:23.090
You planning on acting out 
one of your erotic dojinshi?

10:23.090 --> 10:25.200
No. Who would want to—

10:25.200 --> 10:26.580
<i>...in a romantic sense?</i>

10:27.860 --> 10:30.570
S-Stop it! Quit playing that over and over!

10:32.180 --> 10:34.610
I bet I'll get at least 
a month of fun out of this!

10:34.610 --> 10:35.970
Damn it.

10:35.970 --> 10:38.890
Well, I can see that you've 
given this genuine thought.

10:38.890 --> 10:41.990
I'll let this all be water under the bridge.

10:42.340 --> 10:45.500
Man, that was a quest reward 
I sure didn't expect!

10:45.500 --> 10:47.750
I guess it pays to act out 
every now and then, huh?

10:48.850 --> 10:51.250
You sure change gears quickly.

10:52.450 --> 10:57.690
So, Senpai... this means I'm back 
to being your pesky little Iroha-chan.

10:57.690 --> 11:02.690
But you didn't come here just to 
make me a business offer, did you?

11:02.690 --> 11:04.510
You're quite perceptive.

11:04.510 --> 11:06.140
That's exactly right.

11:07.640 --> 11:09.140
Iroha, I want to ask you,

11:09.510 --> 11:13.200
no, everyone in 05th Floor 
Alliance, for a favor.

11:15.640 --> 11:22.410
<i>I was a fool for thinking even for a second 
that she might have romantic feelings for me.</i>

11:23.240 --> 11:28.910
<b>I LOVE YOU. I LOVE YOU MORE
THAN ANYONE IN THE WORLD.</b>

11:23.790 --> 11:28.590
<i>If she happened to confess to me 
the way Mashiro did...</i>

11:29.180 --> 11:32.420
<i>I would've had to turn down yet another one.</i>

11:32.900 --> 11:38.860
<i>Frankly, I'm relieved I can go back to 
focusing solely on 05th Floor Alliance.</i>

11:41.190 --> 11:44.390
<i>Wait, did she actually think 
that far ahead when...</i>

11:45.050 --> 11:46.410
<i>Was it a cover for...</i>

11:46.810 --> 11:48.810
<i>Nah. Not a chance.</i>

11:49.390 --> 11:51.110
<i>She's Iroha, after all.</i>

11:52.100 --> 11:55.110
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

11:56.860 --> 12:03.290
You have to make a useless drama club 
rank high in a summer competition, huh?

12:04.180 --> 12:07.330
You're always up to something 
interesting, aren't you, Aki?

12:07.330 --> 12:09.960
He's always full of surprises, right?

12:09.960 --> 12:13.830
But personally, I think that thrill 
is what keeps things fun.

12:14.150 --> 12:17.170
This is necessary for 05th Floor Alliance.

12:16.420 --> 12:27.970
Sine! Cosine! Tangent!

12:17.170 --> 12:19.170
Sorry to ask, but I need your help.

12:19.170 --> 12:23.880
If I'm doing this, I'm not gonna let them 
embarrass me with some lame performance.

12:23.880 --> 12:26.800
<b>REHEARSING! DO NOT PEEK!</b>

12:23.880 --> 12:25.880
Yeah, of course.

12:27.970 --> 12:31.040
So the evil producer has come!

12:31.040 --> 12:32.100
Bap.

12:34.350 --> 12:36.510
A hollow mallet...

12:36.510 --> 12:38.060
Is this a drama club prop?

12:38.660 --> 12:41.400
Accept your punishment peacefully, evildoer!

12:41.400 --> 12:44.280
Of course I'm gonna fight back 
if you suddenly try to attack me.

12:45.730 --> 12:47.930
W-Well, it's just not right!

12:47.930 --> 12:51.090
"I'm letting Ohboshi-kun handle 
everything for the drama club."

12:51.090 --> 12:54.920
The very idea of Onee-chan—
Kageishi-sensei saying such a thing!

12:54.920 --> 12:59.040
She's always said she's here 
to nurture our autonomy!

13:01.050 --> 13:04.170
<i>I couldn't convince Midori-chan! Sowwy!</i>

13:04.510 --> 13:07.710
You've clearly made some 
shady deal behind the scenes!

13:07.710 --> 13:09.680
What shady deal?

13:09.680 --> 13:13.040
You wanted to buy out our drama club,

13:13.040 --> 13:16.690
so you... v-violated her...

13:16.690 --> 13:19.570
Didn't you, you animal?!

13:19.570 --> 13:21.190
What am I, a bandit?

13:21.620 --> 13:24.650
I haven't done anything to Sensei.

13:24.650 --> 13:28.880
And what would even I gain from 
buying out this pitiful drama club?

13:28.880 --> 13:30.330
Well...

13:30.330 --> 13:33.830
You could make all of the members 
your sex slaves.

13:35.080 --> 13:37.370
You're actually a pervert, aren't you?

13:37.370 --> 13:41.210
I-I-I am not! Enough of these 
baseless accusations!

13:41.210 --> 13:48.280
Anyway, if you guys want to win 
the competition, you need our help.

13:48.280 --> 13:51.970
Kageishi-sensei made that call after 
giving it plenty of calm, rational thought.

13:52.530 --> 13:55.600
Or do you not trust Sensei's judgment?

13:56.730 --> 13:58.810
But... But...

13:59.620 --> 14:03.740
We've been doing the best 
we can all this time,

14:03.740 --> 14:06.330
only for someone with 
no experience to take over.

14:07.570 --> 14:10.160
How are we supposed to accept that?!

14:10.160 --> 14:11.840
I only saw a brief part of your rehearsal,

14:11.840 --> 14:15.200
but it was clear to me 
how much effort you've all put in.

14:15.200 --> 14:15.910
Huh?

14:16.340 --> 14:19.170
That was exactly what 
made me want to help you.

14:19.170 --> 14:20.860
Ohboshi-kun...

14:21.290 --> 14:24.920
As I see it, this drama club has potential.

14:24.920 --> 14:26.490
You have nowhere to go but up.

14:26.490 --> 14:29.160
Even in this cluttered, unused 
classroom on the fourth floor,

14:29.160 --> 14:31.690
with no specific instruction 
from your advisor,

14:31.690 --> 14:35.240
you still have the tenacity to spend 
your precious lunchtimes rehearsing.

14:35.240 --> 14:39.300
That ridiculous level of dedication 
and effort is honestly worthy of praise.

14:40.930 --> 14:45.080
But results come from multiplying 
the amount of effort you put in

14:41.560 --> 14:47.690
<b>RESULTS = AMOUNT OF EFFORT × DIRECTION OF EFFORT</b>

14:45.080 --> 14:47.080
by the direction of said effort.

14:48.290 --> 14:50.320
You can practically kill yourselves trying,

14:50.320 --> 14:53.970
but if you're not facing the right direction, 
you'll never get positive results.

14:53.970 --> 14:56.200
The results can even be negative.

14:56.600 --> 14:59.830
If you continue as you are, 
you'll end up disbanded for sure.

15:01.330 --> 15:04.090
But I know how to prevent 
that from happening.

15:04.570 --> 15:08.050
If you all put in the effort required, 
you'll be the best around.

15:08.380 --> 15:09.580
I know it.

15:10.680 --> 15:13.640
So take my hand and keep your club alive,

15:13.640 --> 15:15.310
or refuse and be disbanded.

15:15.740 --> 15:17.160
The choice is yours.

15:20.800 --> 15:22.230
President Midori...

15:25.670 --> 15:31.320
And if you can't trust me because you think 
I'm an animal who seduced Sensei,

15:31.710 --> 15:33.570
you're mistaken.

15:33.570 --> 15:36.290
A-Anyone can claim they're innocent!

15:36.290 --> 15:39.200
But I know men are all a bunch of lying wolves!

15:39.490 --> 15:42.020
I can prove it. Right, Ozu?

15:42.700 --> 15:44.320
Yeah, it's true.

15:44.740 --> 15:48.550
The only one Aki considers 
special is me, apparently.

15:52.860 --> 15:56.350
What?! D-Do you mean...

15:56.350 --> 15:59.060
Wait, what was that bestial scream just now?

15:59.060 --> 16:04.730
I-It seems like there was a student 
running around naked and yelling outside.

16:04.730 --> 16:06.410
I'll give them a talking-to later.

16:06.410 --> 16:10.510
<i>I can't believe none of them 
saw through her flimsy excuse.</i>

16:11.070 --> 16:15.530
O-O-Ohboshi-kun... i-is he your, um...

16:15.790 --> 16:18.840
I'm the only one for Aki. Kohinata Ozuma.

16:18.840 --> 16:20.720
Nice to meet you, Kageishi-san.

16:20.720 --> 16:23.670
<i>That was perfect, Ozu. 
Just like we discussed.</i>

16:24.270 --> 16:26.500
Kohinata-kun and Ohboshi-kun...

16:26.500 --> 16:28.590
Y-You two have <i>that</i> kind of relationship?

16:30.980 --> 16:32.970
<i>Well, it's not like any of that was a lie.</i>

16:32.970 --> 16:37.290
<i>Ozu is special to me because 
he's the only one I call a friend.</i>

16:38.010 --> 16:39.950
Do you believe me now?

16:39.950 --> 16:41.820
Oh... Well, um...

16:41.820 --> 16:44.100
F-Fine! I get it!

16:44.100 --> 16:46.160
What you're into is your own business!

16:46.160 --> 16:48.110
I can't say a thing about it!

16:48.110 --> 16:53.600
So you believe there's nothing weird 
between me and Kageishi-sensei, then?

16:53.600 --> 16:55.110
I do.

16:55.110 --> 16:58.780
Then I'm asking you to hear me out.

16:59.430 --> 17:01.210
Very well.

17:01.820 --> 17:03.630
Is that okay with all of you?

17:03.630 --> 17:07.170
If it's okay with you,
 then it's okay with us.

17:07.170 --> 17:08.400
Thanks.

17:14.550 --> 17:18.390
But if I'm not convinced by what you say, 
that's an instant no!

17:18.890 --> 17:20.600
Sure. Not a problem.

17:21.220 --> 17:22.720
Let me introduce these guys.

17:23.070 --> 17:25.160
Kohinata Ozuma, the programmer...

17:25.160 --> 17:26.080
Hi.

17:26.080 --> 17:28.140
...and Otoi-san, the sound engineer.

17:28.140 --> 17:28.730
Yo.

17:29.190 --> 17:31.110
These two will be helping me.

17:31.470 --> 17:35.490
Next, I'll talk about how we'll 
be helping the drama club.

17:35.960 --> 17:40.700
After watching your rehearsal, 
I wrote up a few issues I saw.

17:41.240 --> 17:44.870
<b>PROBLEMS 
1. PERFORMERS' ACTING SKILL 
2. SCREENPLAY 
3. STAGE PRODUCTION 
4. MUSIC AND SOUND</b>

17:41.860 --> 17:43.660
They fit into four broad categories.

17:43.660 --> 17:44.870
That's basically everything!

17:44.870 --> 17:54.130
<b>PROBLEMS 
1. PERFORMERS' ACTING SKILL 
2. SCREENPLAY 
3. STAGE PRODUCTION 
4. MUSIC AND SOUND</b>

17:45.630 --> 17:50.120
If you can't fix all of these, you're unlikely 
to get anywhere in the competition.

17:50.120 --> 17:52.360
Putting your acting skills 
aside for the moment,

17:52.360 --> 17:56.760
the solutions I'd like to propose 
for the other three is...

17:56.760 --> 18:04.860
<b>PROPOSED SOLUTIONS 
1. STRENGTHEN YOUR SCREENPLAY 
-> SWITCH TO A BRAND-NEW SCRIPT</b>

17:57.290 --> 18:03.470
<i>We can rework Makigai Namako-sensei's 
rejected script into a play.</i>

18:03.870 --> 18:05.970
<i>As for the stage setting and sound,</i>

18:04.860 --> 18:12.960
<b>2. STRENGTHEN YOUR STAGE SETTING 
-> KOHINATA OZUMA AND PRESIDENT MIDORI 
WILL WORK TOGETHER TO MAKE SOMETHING NEW</b>

18:05.970 --> 18:10.280
<i>Ozu, Sumire-sensei, and Otoi-san 
can create and supervise.</i>

18:10.700 --> 18:14.930
<i>But we can't let them know 
about Sumire-sensei's other job,</i>

18:12.960 --> 18:21.530
<b>3. STRENGTHEN YOUR MUSIC AND SOUND 
-> OTOI WILL SUPERVISE</b>

18:14.930 --> 18:19.650
<i>so I'll get Murasaki Shikibu-sensei
 to help out remotely.</i>

18:19.650 --> 18:21.180
<i>That's the plan.</i>

18:21.530 --> 18:25.760
Wow... it's like a full-on 
corporate presentation.

18:25.760 --> 18:30.270
Kageishi-sensei did say 
he was an amazing producer.

18:30.270 --> 18:32.670
The stage setting and sound are one thing,

18:32.670 --> 18:35.920
but we can't just suddenly 
switch over to a brand-new play!

18:36.360 --> 18:38.930
If it's a better story than our 
current one, then maybe, but...

18:38.930 --> 18:42.750
Fair enough. It's not a play yet,

18:42.750 --> 18:45.120
but I brought the script 
I intend to use,

18:45.120 --> 18:47.670
so could you give it a quick read 
and see what you think?

18:53.160 --> 18:58.320
This is the event scenario Makigai-sensei 
wrote during that weird period, isn't it?

18:58.610 --> 18:59.500
Yeah.

18:59.500 --> 19:02.200
It turned out much better 
after I had it revised,

19:02.200 --> 19:04.700
but I still didn't think 
they'd find it <i>that</i> moving.

19:05.100 --> 19:07.920
Are these sparkly love stories 
for cute, happy people

19:07.920 --> 19:09.990
the kind of thing high school girls like?

19:11.210 --> 19:12.080
We'll do it!

19:12.080 --> 19:13.940
Please let us use this script!

19:13.940 --> 19:16.100
In fact, I can't imagine anything better!

19:16.100 --> 19:17.940
Well, I do feel that way, but...

19:17.940 --> 19:18.840
But?

19:18.840 --> 19:22.320
We're the ones in charge of the stage setting,

19:22.780 --> 19:26.420
and it would be kind of difficult 
to suddenly change our play now.

19:26.420 --> 19:28.640
It'd be one thing if it were 
just some small props,

19:28.640 --> 19:31.780
but if you're talking about changing 
our backgrounds and larger props,

19:31.780 --> 19:34.220
we don't have the time or the budget.

19:34.220 --> 19:36.840
I can take care of that for you.

19:37.630 --> 19:42.380
We should be able to cover all your 
backgrounds with projection mapping.

19:42.380 --> 19:45.740
I think I can make something in three days 
if I pull an all-nighter or two.

19:45.740 --> 19:47.580
What? Really?

19:47.580 --> 19:49.500
Yep. This is what he does.

19:49.500 --> 19:52.140
And we'll figure out something 
for the larger props.

19:52.140 --> 19:54.850
Do you think you can 
take charge of the small props?

19:54.850 --> 19:56.720
That much, we can do!

19:56.720 --> 19:58.670
We'll put our all into making them perfect!

19:58.990 --> 20:01.860
<i>And that takes care of 
the stage setting problem.</i>

20:01.860 --> 20:03.180
<i>As for the sound and music...</i>

20:03.770 --> 20:06.400
Do you have videos of your past plays?

20:06.400 --> 20:08.750
Yes, we have a recording of last year's.

20:08.750 --> 20:11.470
<i>I think we can leave that in Otoi-san's hands.</i>

20:11.470 --> 20:13.440
Okay, let's start by looking at that.

20:13.440 --> 20:15.280
That just leaves the acting.

20:15.280 --> 20:17.620
Acting isn't something 
we can change substantially

20:17.620 --> 20:20.040
just because of some outside criticism.

20:20.040 --> 20:22.050
Do you have some sort of secret plan?

20:22.050 --> 20:23.450
Yeah, of course.

20:23.450 --> 20:29.830
<b>PROBLEMS 
1. PERFORMERS' ACTING SKILL 
2. SCREENPLAY</b>

20:23.880 --> 20:25.820
I'll have the actors in the play

20:25.820 --> 20:29.450
head to a different room for some 
intensive lessons, starting now.

20:30.120 --> 20:32.580
Intensive lessons?

20:32.580 --> 20:36.960
We can't be taught by just anyone, you know.

20:36.960 --> 20:38.090
Not a problem.

20:38.580 --> 20:40.970
You'll understand the moment you meet her.

20:42.090 --> 20:43.530
So you've finally arrived.

20:44.450 --> 20:46.140
This is your instructor.

20:48.350 --> 20:51.350
Her? Just who is she?

20:54.740 --> 20:57.610
You can just call me "Instructor."

20:58.040 --> 21:01.640
She looks pretty shady. 
Are you sure about this?

21:01.640 --> 21:04.980
I need to keep her name and 
face secret, because reasons.

21:04.980 --> 21:07.930
But I promise you, her acting skill is real.

21:07.930 --> 21:10.740
You must be the club president,
 Kageishi Midori-san.

21:10.740 --> 21:14.140
What's important is not who I am,

21:14.140 --> 21:17.630
but how well I can act,
 wouldn't you agree?

21:18.250 --> 21:20.490
Yes, that is true.

21:20.490 --> 21:22.890
All right, let's see what you can do.

21:22.890 --> 21:26.500
I'll decide whether or not 
you're a worthy instructor by your acting!

21:29.090 --> 21:30.180
But of course.

21:30.180 --> 21:33.310
<i>With Iroha handling this, we can't fail.</i>

21:33.310 --> 21:36.240
<i>Go on, show them the very soul of acting!</i>

21:37.240 --> 21:41.440
Then I will act out a scene 
from the script you received today.

21:41.440 --> 21:44.570
A scene? Not just one part?

21:46.300 --> 21:48.480
Just watch and learn.

21:51.660 --> 21:55.540
<b>Translation: Becky Cottrill</b>

21:55.910 --> 21:59.000
<b>Subtitle Editing: Geoff Mazzolini
Subtitle Timing: Krzysztof Kunc</b>

21:59.540 --> 22:02.880
<b>Quality Control: Gabriella Ramirez
Translation Check: David Saylor</b>

23:23.210 --> 23:26.210
<b>DON'T MISS THE NEXT EPISODE!!!</b>

23:23.840 --> 23:26.210
<b>SO PRECIOUS!</b>
